# LF in the repository and LF in the working copy, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` checks
# every source file out with CRLF endings, and `npm run format:check` fails on
# a clean clone before anyone has typed a character — Prettier normalises to LF
# and would report all 78 files as needing formatting. Which trains people to
# ignore the check, on their own machine, forever.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever the extension heuristics think.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
